Backport of upstream NUT commit edc06fb39435b892d5daeec53cb4845cb12d1d50
(PR #3550, issue #3136) for a stack out-of-bounds read in the USB driver
open path. No CVE was assigned, so this patch has no VEX entry and no
SBOM-fragment analysis entry, unlike the CVE-2026-54161 backport.

nut_libusb_open() chooses between two candidate HID report descriptor
lengths held in `int32_t rdlens[2]`, but bounds both the loop and the
"ran out of candidates" check with sizeof(rdlens) (8, the byte size)
instead of the element count (2):

	for (j = 0; j < sizeof(rdlens); j++)

Iterations 2..7 read 24 bytes past the end of the array and use that
stack garbage as rdlen. Garbage that happens to pass the rdlen sanity
checks is passed to the USB control transfer and on to the HID parser
callback, which is where upstream saw it segfault.

The out-of-range indices are reached only when neither real candidate
worked, that is when both descriptor reads failed. That is the state a
wedged or mid-re-enumeration USB UPS presents, which is the failure this
image's comms watchdog exists to recover from. The watchdog's recovery
restarts the driver straight back into this code path, so the defect sits
on the recovery path rather than off it.

Regression from upstream aba6f43544b17d2f16e69ca19f162c6c19748fc7 ("if
the tried 'rdlen' did not succeed, fall back to the other value we had in
mind"), first released in v2.8.5, so this pinned version is the first
affected one. SIZEOF_ARRAY() is already defined in v2.8.5's
include/common.h, which both files include.

Both libusb backends carry the identical defect and upstream fixed both.
This image compiles the libusb-1.0 backend, so drivers/libusb1.c is the
file that ships: the running container reports "USB communication driver
(libusb 1.0) 0.53" at driver start and "driver.version.usb:
libusb-1.0.30" in upsc output. The libusb0.c hunks are kept so the patch
stays correct if the build ever resolves the 0.1 API instead.

Remove this patch when NUT_VERSION moves to v2.8.6+, which ships the fix.
Removal spans three coupled sites: this file, the Dockerfile COPY/apply
step, and the README's "Dependency CVE posture" paragraph that names the
two carried backports. See CONTRIBUTING ("Upstream sources may carry
checked-in patches").

diff --git a/drivers/libusb0.c b/drivers/libusb0.c
index 52f08f2..8471136 100644
--- a/drivers/libusb0.c
+++ b/drivers/libusb0.c
@@ -651,7 +651,7 @@ static int nut_libusb_open(usb_dev_handle **udevp,
 				}
 			}
 
-			for (j = 0; j < sizeof(rdlens); j++) {
+			for (j = 0; j < SIZEOF_ARRAY(rdlens); j++) {
 				rdlen = rdlens[j];
 				if (rdlen < 0)
 					continue;
@@ -716,7 +716,7 @@ static int nut_libusb_open(usb_dev_handle **udevp,
 				break;
 			}
 
-			if (j >= sizeof(rdlens)) {
+			if (j >= SIZEOF_ARRAY(rdlens)) {
 				/* Ended the loop without success */
 				goto next_device;
 			}
diff --git a/drivers/libusb1.c b/drivers/libusb1.c
index b02da58..e9f6c85 100644
--- a/drivers/libusb1.c
+++ b/drivers/libusb1.c
@@ -807,7 +807,7 @@ static int nut_libusb_open(libusb_device_handle **udevp,
 			}
 		}
 
-		for (j = 0; j < sizeof(rdlens); j++) {
+		for (j = 0; j < SIZEOF_ARRAY(rdlens); j++) {
 			rdlen = rdlens[j];
 			if (rdlen < 0)
 				continue;
@@ -897,7 +897,7 @@ static int nut_libusb_open(libusb_device_handle **udevp,
 			break;
 		}
 
-		if (j >= sizeof(rdlens)) {
+		if (j >= SIZEOF_ARRAY(rdlens)) {
 			/* Ended the loop without success */
 			goto next_device;
 		}
